            "category": "technology",
            "title": "Ask HN: How do you find meaning of life at 41?",
            "description": "<p>Happy Thanksgiving!<p>This question crossed my mind in the morning. It feels like I have seen pretty much everything under the Sun. I have modest house (still renting), small kids, a okayish job. I spent time on daily activities and occassionally on long walks.<p>The progress with AI and impact on Software is frankly exciting and depressing at the same time.<p>What are people my age doing these days? How do you keep yourself excited for the future and not feel anxious?<p>Curious to see from a bit older people here how are you doing and challenging yourself well into 40s, 50s and 60s.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50657957\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50657957</a></p>\n<p>Points: 23</p>\n<p># Comments: 32</p>",
